<title>INDIA: India produces 3,835T copper cathodes in January.</title>
<headline>India produces 3,835T copper cathodes in January.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's state-run Hindustan Copper Ltd (HCL) produced 3,835 tonnes of copper cathodes in January 1997 compared to 4,290 tonnes in December 1996, a government statement said on Monday.</p>
<p>HCL also produced 2,700 tonnes of continous cast copper rods in January 1997 against 5,051 tonnes in December 1996, the statement said. The statement said January output fell due to shutdown between January 19 and 29 to replace refractory bricks.</p>
<p>	    Installed     January, 1997   Cumulative output</p>
<p>	    capacity</p>
<p>	    (annual)	 Actual	   Apr96-Jan97  Apr95-Jan96</p>
<p>Copper</p>
<p> cathodes   47,500	 3,835	     30,632	 32,893</p>
<p>Copper</p>
<p> rods	 60,000	 2,700	     33,857	 28,242</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures are in tonnes and provisional.</p>
</text>
